              "type": "text",
              "value": "CHAIR — MODELLING PLAN (surface draft; to be refined)\nMetres unless stated; values in braces are this object's parameters. Z up, floor at Z 0. Hosted on a point: origin at the placement point on the floor.\n\nWHAT IT IS\nmodern upholstered dining armchair, tub back wrapping into arms, diamond quilting, piped seams, splayed oak legs\n\nGEOMETRY\nModel the object described above as clean, closed meshes with real thickness and small bevels on exposed edges (about 2 mm) so highlights catch. Drive every dimension from these parameters:\n- Overall width: {width}\n- Overall depth: {depth}\n- Seat height: {seatHeight}\n- Seat body thickness: {cushionThk}\n- Back height above the seat: {backTop}\n- Arms: {armStyle} (one of: Tub arms / Low arms / Armless)\n- Arm height (from floor): {armHeight}\n- Shell thickness: {shellThk}\n- Back wrap (share of half-width): {backCurve}\n- Back rake (deg): {backRake}\n- Inner back quilting: {quilting} (one of: Diamond / Channel / Plain)\n- Quilt pitch (m): {quiltPitch}\n- Quilt diamond height / width: {quiltAspect}\n- Quilt puff depth (m): {quiltDepth}\n- Piping on the seams: {piping}\n- Piping diameter (m): {pipingDia}\n- Leg diameter at the top: {legSize}\n- Leg diameter at the foot: {legFootDia}\n- Leg splay (deg): {legSplay}\n- Rotation (deg): {rotation}\n- Anchor Direction: {anchorDir} (one of: Top-Left / Top-Center / Top-Right / Left-Center / Center / Right-Center / Bottom-Left / Bottom-Center / Bottom-Right)\n- Margin from host: {margin}\n- Flip side: {flipSide}\nKeep the proportions of a well-made real product; add the secondary detail a close-up render needs (joints, reveals, fixings) but no hidden interior geometry.\n\nMATERIALS\n- Base colour: {baseColor}\n- Roughness: {roughness}\nPrincipled BSDF per visible part, using the colour and roughness above for the main surface; secondary parts in a neutral complementary finish. Use Object / box-projected texture coordinates (no UVs needed). Add a subtle noise bump (strength ~0.03) so surfaces are not perfectly flat.\n\nLIGHTS\nNone. This object does not emit light.\n\nCHECKS (measure after building)\n- Overall width = {width}\n- Overall depth = {depth}\n- Seat height = {seatHeight}\n- Arm height (from floor) = {armHeight}\n- Quilt puff depth (m) = {quiltDepth}\n- Leg diameter at the top = {legSize}\n- All meshes closed, no duplicate faces, origin as stated above.",
